---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { sitePath } from '../lib/urls';
---

<Page
  article
  title="Terms draft: preview use and limitations"
  description="MutualLens preview scope, source completeness limits, permitted own-account use, local storage responsibilities, and unresolved production requirements."
>
  <p class="eyebrow">TERMS · PREVIEW DRAFT</p><h1>Understand the preview.</h1><p
    class="lede"
  >
    MutualLens is experimental software for inspecting supplied follower and
    following data. These draft terms have not been presented as legally
    reviewed. Updated September 7, 2026.
  </p>
  <h2>Use accounts you own or manage</h2><p>
    Use the preview with information you are authorized to process. The intended
    purpose is understanding your own or managed accounts, not covert
    monitoring, bypassing private-account controls, or collecting data for
    resale.
  </p>
  <h2>Availability and accuracy</h2><p>
    Automatic checking is unavailable. Sample data is synthetic and does not
    represent a live account. Local reports describe supplied files and may
    differ from current Instagram state. Partial or unverified inputs cannot
    support definitive absence claims.
  </p><p>
    The preview does not promise unlimited capacity, uninterrupted availability,
    complete platform coverage, or a particular result. It does not automate
    unfollowing or determine why a relationship changed.
  </p>
  <h2>Your local copies</h2><p>
    You control whether to save snapshots and download reports. You are
    responsible for choosing an appropriate device and handling downloaded
    files. Clearing app-controlled snapshots does not remove copies elsewhere.
  </p>
  <h2>No affiliation</h2><p>
    MutualLens is an independent project by Arhaan Aggarwal, not an Instagram or
    Meta product. Instagram and Meta names are used descriptively.
  </p>
  <h2>Before a public production launch</h2><p>
    The automatic acquisition and recurring zero-cash gates, provider
    conditions, production runtime, dedicated contact channel, and applicable
    legal and advertising requirements must be resolved. This preview does not
    represent that those steps have happened.
  </p>
  <p>
    See the <a href={sitePath('/privacy/')}>privacy draft</a> and <a
      href={sitePath('/contact/')}>project contact information</a
    >.
  </p>
</Page>
